From 21b2c89bb86847ebaf708118fc29e38b4fb3bd86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <dongchenchen2@huawei.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:39:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sched: shard task lists by NUMA domain

Adapt the tasklist work in numa-domain-v2-patches (0001-0024 and 0029),
originally by robin <robin800601@gmail.com>, to this tree's task lifetime.

Put process leaders on permanent NUMA lists and keep every thread on its
leader's home shard across migration and nonleader exec. Fork, release and
exit notification take only their home shard. Snapshot readers and cold
cross-process writers take all shards in a fixed order.

Complete reparenting and tracer-exit serialization before removing their
all-shard exclusion. Group state locks protect parent/ptrace transitions;
parent links locks serialize children and ptraced lists. Reparent nests
group locks in parent-before-child order, takes links locks by address,
and rechecks pinned reapers against PF_EXITING. Tracer exit drops its links
lock before taking a tracee's group lock. Fork protects its unpublished
child until all links, PIDs and tracing state are ready.

Walk subreaper trees with RCU lookups and pinned groups, without a global
tasklist reader. Serialize only concurrent walks, retain visited entries,
and exclude reparenting while marking a group and queueing its children.
Use separate subreaper boolean fields and inherit under the links lock.
Pin notification parents and their PIDs, and acquire sighand safely.
Publish EXIT_ZOMBIE after the exec wakeup and claim autoreap with cmpxchg,
including the reparented-zombie fix from patch 0029. Serialize orphan-group
decisions with a per-PGID lock when parent relationships can affect them.

Use a separate PID task-membership lock: reusing the proc inode lock under
sighand introduces an IRQ lock inversion. Convert fork/thread counters and
all consumers, including BPF RVI and s390 appldata, to atomic operations.
Publish namespace reapers atomically while allowing the init_task sentinel.
Update iteration, the early cgroup assertion and debugfs domain counts.

Model the shard set as one tasklist lockdep identity, preserving external
ordering without a held-lock entry per node. Keep offline shards visible
and retain the ordinary rwlock fallback for early boot, UP and PREEMPT_RT.

Validated with an x86_64 NUMA lockdep build and two-node QEMU lifecycle,
ptrace, pidfd, clone3 and CPU-hotplug tests, plus UP and SMP !NUMA object
builds. The pre-existing vmaccess attach timeout is excluded explicitly.

Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <dongchenchen2@huawei.com>
